1
00:43:17,200 --> 00:43:25,852
God's love is displayed upon the cross;

2
00:43:25,852 --> 00:43:34,703
for me the Lord endured torment and scorn,

3
00:43:34,703 --> 00:43:43,006
shamed by men,

4
00:43:43,006 --> 00:43:49,115
heaped with slander.

5
00:43:49,115 --> 00:43:54,725
The Father's beloved Son tasted

6
00:43:54,725 --> 00:44:00,335
every mockery and torment,

7
00:44:00,335 --> 00:44:05,875
crowned with thorns,

8
00:44:05,875 --> 00:44:12,801
and cruelly scourged,

9
00:44:12,801 --> 00:44:24,021
His body covered over with wounds.

10
00:44:24,021 --> 00:44:29,561
Hands and feet nailed fast,

11
00:44:29,561 --> 00:44:36,488
hung high upon the wood,

12
00:44:36,488 --> 00:44:41,475
in utter agony —

13
00:44:41,475 --> 00:44:47,708
who can feel it?

14
00:45:01,421 --> 00:45:38,796
The pain that never ceases.

15
00:45:38,796 --> 00:45:45,354
His face gaunt and wasted,

16
00:45:45,354 --> 00:45:54,080
hung on the cross, His bones now all laid bare,

17
00:45:54,080 --> 00:46:03,256
blood streaming down His face,

18
00:46:03,256 --> 00:46:09,040
dripping to the ground,

19
00:46:09,040 --> 00:46:11,982
sorely wounded,

20
00:46:11,982 --> 00:46:20,460
yet struck even by the Father.

21
00:46:20,460 --> 00:46:25,779
Who could write a poem

22
00:46:25,779 --> 00:46:32,428
to capture such love?

23
00:46:32,428 --> 00:46:37,636
His love,

24
00:46:37,636 --> 00:46:44,146
engraved within my heart.

25
00:46:44,146 --> 00:46:49,410
How fresh His mercy,

26
00:46:49,410 --> 00:46:55,990
deep and wide —

27
00:46:55,990 --> 00:47:00,976
the grace of the cross,

28
00:47:00,976 --> 00:47:07,210
who can ever fathom it?

29
00:47:07,210 --> 00:47:12,196
My Lord even

30
00:47:12,196 --> 00:47:18,430
cried out, "It is finished."

31
00:47:18,430 --> 00:47:29,650
I will ponder it ten thousand times over.

32
00:47:29,650 --> 00:47:35,190
Jesus, my Lord,

33
00:47:35,190 --> 00:47:42,116
Your love runs deep and will never die.

34
00:47:42,116 --> 00:47:47,103
This grace

35
00:47:47,103 --> 00:47:53,336
forever moves us.

36
00:47:53,336 --> 00:48:06,900
This deep grace — come, and feel it.
